#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / dpkg Specification
PACKAGE: dpkg
LANGUAGE: C
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Local package database and low-level package transaction engine

## PROGRAM
dpkg owns local package state, package unpack/configure/remove operations, and maintainer-script execution within the Debian package model.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Ubuntu/Debian dpkg source
BOUNDARY: package archive -> metadata validation -> database -> unpack/configure -> scripts -> recorded state
WHITE_EDITION: controlled overlay
GUI: inspection/administration frontend may call supported operations; it must not bypass dpkg

## SPEC
- preserve package database integrity
- make interrupted operations recoverable
- retain package provenance and state
- preserve maintainer-script compatibility
- expose failures without concealing transaction state

## QUALITY
TEST: install, upgrade, remove, malformed metadata, script failure, interrupted transaction, recovery, database consistency
ECONOMY: database size, transaction duration, memory, process behavior

## SOURCE POLICY
Dpkg is primarily C. Native changes require a concrete correctness/security requirement and regression coverage. Package-format compatibility is a hard boundary.
